<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>server_rack_4</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>

  <author>
    <name>spot_gazebo_ros2</name>
  </author>

  <description>
    42U server rack, partially populated / mid-commissioning configuration.
    27U occupied, 15U empty spread across six separate gaps. A 10RU blade
    chassis dominates the middle; the rest is sparse edge gear.
    11 RFID tags (rfid_tag_r4_*), EPC block E200-4001..E200-400B.

    The sparse case, and the inverse of rack 2. Tags are far apart, so read
    attribution is easy, but 15U of genuine air means a reader that treats
    "no read" as "occluded" rather than "empty" will over-report inventory.
    This is the rack that exercises the report_n_tags ground-truth leak: with
    only 11 tags against rack 2's 23, an estimator leaning on the reported tag
    count will look much better here than it deserves to.
  </description>
</model>
